      "key": "descri",
      "label": "Summary",
      "searchable": true,
      "value": "Flyer and poster for the theatrical production “Cuba libre: A musical celebration,” presented by INTAR Hispanic American Arts Center in New York City in 1995 as part of its 30th anniversary season. The production featured music and performance celebrating Cuban cultural traditions, with choreography by Alberto Alonso and direction by Max Ferrá. The materials include cast listings, production credits, performance dates, and promotional design elements.\n"
    },
    {
      "controlledVocab": false,
      "controlledVocabList": null,
      "key": "note",
      "label": "Note",
      "searchable": true,
      "value": "Performances held from October 26 through December 3, 1995, at INTAR Theater, 420 West 42nd Street, New York City. Includes ticketing information and references to INTAR’s 30th anniversary programming. For other related materials please contact Cuban Heritage Collection."
    },
